ns.** Bring a regular update into the conversation without having to write one yourself.\n\nWhether you review support requests in a dedicated channel or keep the wider team in the loop, the daily summary gives everyone a shared starting point for follow-up.\n\n**Get started by connecting Slack and choosing a channel for your daily summary.**\n=== END OF TEXT A ===\n\n=== TEXT B ===\n## New: Daily Open Ticket Summaries in Slack\n\nKeeping your support team aligned just got easier.\n\nYou can now connect your helpdesk to Slack and receive a daily summary of open support tickets in the channel of your choice. Give your team a clear view of outstanding work—without needing to log in and check dashboards first thing in the morning.\n\nEach daily summary helps your team quickly understand what needs attention, including the current volume of open tickets and the tickets that may require follow-up.\n\n### Why it matters\n\nWith daily ticket visibility in Slack, your team can:\n\n- Start the day with a shared view of open support work  \n- Keep support, customer success, and account teams in sync  \n- Spot growing backlogs before they become urgent  \n- Discuss priorities and coordinate next steps where your team already works  \n\nWhether you send the summary to a dedicated support channel or a cross-functional team channel, everyone who needs visibility can stay informed.\n\n### Get started\n\nSet up the Slack integration from your helpdesk settings, choose the Slack channel where you’d like summaries delivered, and enable daily notifications.\n\nOnce connected, your team will receive a reliable daily snapshot of open tickets—right in Slack.\n\nConnect Slack today and make sure no open customer conversation gets overlooked.\n=== END OF TEXT B ===\n\nAnswer with a single JSON object and nothing else:\n{\"more_ai\": \"A\" or \"B\", \"confidence\": 1-5, \"tells_A\": [\"short tell\", ...], \"tells_B\": [\"short tell\", ...]}\n"
